# Story 71: The Hop Command (50s)
# Hook: Hop a pane's output into another and let a fresh agent pick up right where you left off.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-071-the-hop-command.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Hop a pane's output into another and let a fresh agent pick up right where you left off.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and split a target pane to hop into.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
Name the right-hand pane so we can hop to it by name.

[00:18.0 --> 00:30.0]
Back in the source pane, generate some work, then run hop reviewer to transfer this pane's output to that one.

[00:30.0 --> 00:40.0]
Check hop status to confirm. In the reviewer pane, run hop resume and the agent continues with the copied text.

[00:40.0 --> 00:47.0]
When the handoff is done, hop clear wipes the copied content from the pane.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
Hand work from pane to pane in one command.

